<p>Students should compare the latest counselling brochure, seat matrix and round-wise allotment if the college participates in a centralised process. If admission is merit-based or direct, ask the admission office for the current selection rule and whether seats are filled first-come, merit-list based or through counselling.</p>' ELSE cutoff END,
  rankings_content = '<h3>Rankings, Approvals And Recognition</h3>
<p>Bharathiyar Arts and Science College for Women - [BASCW], Salem ranking and approval claims are kept conservative in this profile. The production record mentions NAAC, UGC. Students should verify approvals through the relevant official regulator, affiliating university or institutional disclosure.</p>
<p>No current national ranking claim is added in this pass unless a recognised ranking source is available.</p>
<p>NAAC grade is not expanded without a checked validity period.</p>
<p>For trusted comparison, DekhoCampus prioritises official institute pages, regulator records, NIRF or other recognised ranking pages, university affiliation lists and mandatory disclosures. Third-party summaries may help orientation, but they should not override official records for admission, course and fee decisions.</p>',
  facilities_content = '<h3>Facilities And Campus Support</h3>
<p>Bharathiyar Arts and Science College for Women - [BASCW], Salem facilities should be checked by department and student need. A campus may have a library, labs or activity spaces, but the real question is whether those facilities are accessible, maintained and relevant to the selected programme.</p>
<ul><li>Library</li><li>Classrooms</li><li>Student support</li><li>Department facilities</li><li>Campus assistance</li></ul>
<p>Students should confirm library timing, laboratory access, equipment condition, classroom quality, internet availability, student grievance support, medical assistance, sports access, safety arrangements and transport. For professional programmes, practical labs, workshops, clinical exposure, design studios or teaching-practice arrangements matter more than a generic facility list.</p>',
